  "_comment": "Adaptive scheduler with startup trim (--adapt-startup-trim: until the limit first holds a request back, each evaluation lowers it to 1 + peak in-flight requests). Without it, starting at c = 10 only matched the hand-tuned FIFO c = 6 (P95 +4% +- 12) instead of the -9% of starting at c = 5, because the unused limit stayed at 10 through the light first ~100 s and the first burst was admitted at 10. 5 slots + 4 GiB host cache, W1 0.95X, seeds 42-44, starting at c = 10 (should now match the c = 5 start) and at c = 5 (should be unchanged), six runs, ~1.5 h. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_p5_cram results/phase2_adaptive results/phase2_adaptive_start10 results/phase2_adaptive_trim --label-key concurrency cache_ram_mb load_pct_x --baseline 6_p5/4096/95 --ignore experiment phase policy",
